From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReplayMod-LegacyFabric <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:15:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Drive jGui's event callbacks from Mixins on 1.8.9 Fabric

jGui gets its screen, input, tick and HUD events from Forge on <=1.12 and
from 1.14+ specific Mixins on Fabric. Fabric on 1.8.9 has neither, and no
loader API providing them, so:

- gate the Forge event bus and the 1.14+ Mixins to what they were written for
- add ScreenInputCallback, the equivalent of Forge's Mouse/KeyboardInputEvent.Pre
- add 1.8.9-fabric Mixins which fire the existing callbacks
- ignore input in wrappers of vanilla screens that are no longer current
- don't declare IOException on overrides, Legacy Yarn dropped it

